[00:02.34]Title: The White Noise
[00:07.63](Cut-up corporate jingle, chipper but unsettling):
[00:10.83]"For peace of mind, and thoughts aligned... trust 'Dimensional Holdings Inc.'... We own your inner space..."
[01:09.59]Yo, the quantum foam is bubbling, the subatomic dust is thick,
[01:12.35]We’re charting vectors past the known, where the axiomatic stick
[01:14.87]Snaps clean from the foundation, the architect is gone,
[01:17.28]Just the ghosts in the machine humming till the break of dawn.
[01:19.61]CERN’s cathedral humming low, a synthesized Gregorian chant,
[01:22.29]Smash the particles, see the void, the covenant we can’t
[01:24.76]Decipher in the daylight, under fluorescent blight,
[01:26.87]We’re mining for the *Loosh* that fuels the engine of the night.
[01:29.06]Mary Brennan’s faded portrait, now a plastic daisy bloom,
[01:31.40]A spectral data point dissolving in the vacuum of the room.
[01:34.04]EVP captured whispers, static coded in the black,
[01:36.43]The agents of entropy are lining up to take the track.
[01:38.46][Trash
[01:38.46]The spark is hidden.
[01:48.51]It’s the white noise frequency, the signal we can’t mute,
[01:51.08]The fractal pattern screaming from the undiscovered root.
[01:53.50]We’re feeding the machine, this *Feast* beneath the ashes and the dust
[01:56.02]A chemical euphoria built on broken, brittle trust.
[01:58.43]The Frenzy hits the system, every synapse overloaded,
[02:00.70]"Just Wait…" the promise whispered, while the timeline’s being coded.
[02:03.22]We breach the Astral veil, chasing shadows of the alien script,
[02:05.91]Every iteration looping, every fragile secret stripped.
[02:37.22]The dark matter hums a rhythm, a metronome of dread,
[02:39.85]While the silver-laced delusion floats inside my heavy head.
[02:42.30]That crystalline compulsion, yeah, the meth-fueled pilgrimage,
[02:44.96]To see the schematics flicker on the monitor’s edge.
[02:47.05]They say it’s infrastructure, but I hear the alien tongue,
[02:49.48]The phantom signal bleeding where the logic has unstrung.
[02:51.94]E.T.!!—the three-letter cipher for the void that stares right back,
[02:54.51]Through the lens of the collider, on the super-heated track.
[02:57.12]We’re tearing at the fabric, looking for the seam to pull,
[02:59.37]To find the source of the sorrow that makes the human spirit dull.
[03:01.96]The entropy agents are the janitors of failing states,
[03:04.36]Cleaning up the residue when the grand experiment abates.
[03:06.76]It’s the white noise frequency, the signal we can’t mute,
[03:09.45]The fractal pattern screaming from the undiscovered root.
[03:11.73]We’re feeding the machine, this *Feast* beneath the earth’s cold crust,
[03:14.38]A chemical euphoria built on broken, brittle trust.
[03:16.84]The Frenzy hits the system, every synapse overloaded,
[03:19.16]"Just Wait…" the promise whispered, while the timeline’s being coded.
[03:21.75]We breach the Astral veil, chasing shadows of the alien script,
[03:24.48]Every iteration looping, every fragile secret stripped.
[04:26.44]"...and the Watchers shall lease out the very dreams of men, for a pittance of silver and shadow."
[04:41.95]The geometry is wrong, the angles start to bend,
[04:44.41]This ain't physics, this is prophecy that finds no end.
[04:46.68]They siphon off the psychic residue, the *Loosh* they crave to hoard,
[04:49.53]While Mary Brennan’s daisy wilts upon the particle board.
[04:52.11]We’re living in the echo of a signal yet to land,
[04:54.21]A million frequencies colliding in this subterranean sand.
[04:57.08]The agents are laughing, they know the final score,
[04:59.56]It’s just another cycle, then we start to ask for more.
